[VERDICTS]
  TESTABILITY: BELOW SENSITIVITY.  max |1+w0| 2.97e-06 = 5.4e-05 sigma(w0) [0.055, context]; max |wa| 1.60e-05 = 7.7e-05 sigma(wa) [0.208]; max |dlog10 a0| (z <= 3) 6.66e-07 dex = 9.5e-05 of 0.007 dex (3.3e-05 of the record's unseparable 0.02 dex; 4.4e-06 of the 0.15 dex per-disc floor).
  Statistical-only disc count to see the z = 2 drift at 0.1 dex per disc: N ~ 3.7e+10 (before any systematic floor).
  SIGN: PHANTOM-SIDE: Q >= 0 at every z (ratchet), so rho_DE grows toward today, 1 + w_DE = -q <= 0, no crossing of -1. max q (z <= 3) = 9.90e-07.
  Canonical partner: phi'' + 3H phi' + V' = Q/phi' is singular at phi' = 0 (w = -1). The source is a small perturbation only where 1 + w_phi >> q ~ 1e-06; the observed w_eff = w_phi - q. So a canonical partner can show w_eff < -1 only inside a band |1 + w| <~ 1e-06 around -1, i.e. the sink cannot produce or rescue an O(0.1) crossing of -1; with w_phi exactly -1 it is singular.
  CFG511 fork (a0 tracking -p_DE instead of rho_DE) under this prediction: <= 1.6e-07 dex.
